---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_DATA } from '../constants';
import portraitImage from '../assets/portrait.png';

import '../styles/about.css';
---

<Layout pageTitle="About">
    <div class="page-container">
        <h1>About me</h1>

        <div class="about-content">
            <div class="about-intro-wrapper centered-column">
                <div class="about-header centered-column">
                    <Image src={portraitImage} alt={SITE_DATA.name} class="about-portrait" />
                    <h2 class="about-name">{SITE_DATA.name}</h2>
                </div>

                <p class="intro-text">
                    Hi, I'm Gabriella Joy, but you can call me Gaby. I’m a frontend software engineer who loves the magic of taking lines of code and turning them into something tangible, beautiful, and alive. 
                    <br/><br/>
                    My engineering journey really took off at Fastly, where I started as an intern and returned full-time to continue learning. Because I have a deep love for design, the frontend is my sweet spot—I thrive on making things look stunning, seamless, 
                    and user-friendly using React and TypeScript. To me, coding isn't just logic; it's a visual art form.
                    <br/><br/>
                    When I’m not at my desk, my creativity doesn't stop. You can usually find me experimenting with makeup looks, sewing, spinning pottery, dancing Hula and Tahitian, or practicing Pilates. I also love doing tarot readings and making time for the people who matter most: my family and friends.
                </p>
            </div>

            <section>
                <h2>Positions</h2>
                <ul class="work-list icon-list">
                    <li>
                        <div class="list-entry">
                            <h3>Software Development Engineer, Fastly</h3>
                            <p class="institution">San Francisco, CA | 2024–present</p>
                            <ul class="custom-list">
                                <li>Mentored incoming engineering interns via pair programming, technical unblocking, and mock presentation reviews to accelerate workplace onboarding</li>
                                <li>Developed responsive web pages, interactive charts, and reusable UI components</li>
                                <li>Resolved critical accessibility (a11y) defects</li>
                                <li>collaborated with product and design to align technical scope with UX requirements</li>
                                <li>Leveraged AI developer tooling (Claude Code, Gemini) to accelerate legacy UI migrations and streamline complex bug resolution</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <div class="list-entry">
                            <h3>Software Engineer Intern, Fastly</h3>
                            <p class="institution">San Francisco, CA | May 2023 - August 2023</p>
                            <ul class="custom-list">
                                <li>Built reusable React components using Typescript and Storybook to provide quick access to customer configuration</li>
                                <li>Developed Mirage mock API endpoints to fetch testing data dynamically</li>
                                <li>Implemented screen reader accessibility into UI components to ensure all users can view content</li>
                                <li>Wrote detailed documentation on outdated code including its logic and bugs/errors to improve future performance</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <div class="list-entry">
                            <h3>CodeDay Labs Intern, CodeDay Labs</h3>
                            <p class="institution">Remote | May 2022 - August 2022</p>
                            <ul class="custom-list">
                                <li>Worked on ForestGEO web application which collects data on trees from 70+ research sites, to improve workflow and advance data analysis for ForestGEO scientists</li>
                                <li>Developed reusable frontend UI components with React and Storybook to collect and validate data</li>
                                <li>Actively participated in weekly meetings, peer code reviews, and daily standup check-ins</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <div class="list-entry">
                            <h3>Math Tutor, Diablo Valley Community College</h3>
                            <p class="institution">Pleasant Hill, CA | January 2020 - April 2020</p>
                            <ul class="custom-list">
                                <li>Tutored students with math as high as multivariable calculus</li>
                                <li>Worked closely with Professors &amp; other tutors to solve problems</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Education</h2>
                <ul class="education-list icon-list">
                    <li>
                        <div class="education-entry">
                            <h3>B.S. in Computer Science</h3>
                            <p class="institution">San Francisco State University, May 2024</p>
                            <p class="grade">Member of Society of Women Engineers</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <div class="education-entry">
                            <h3>A.S. in Computer Science</h3>
                            <p class="institution">Diablo Valley Community College, May 2021</p>
                            <p class="grade">Dean's List - Member of Friends MESA Club</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>
